        "id": 1000436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-28T14:20:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "its initial value is set to 0 on omci_device creation and upon issuing a reset (see above and below).  At either of those points the _mib_data_sync value is both 0 in the omci library and on the onu:\n\n \u003e omci debug --dump 2\nDump OntData in MDM\n  \u003cOntData\u003e\n    \u003cManagedEntityId\u003e0\u003c/ManagedEntityId\u003e\n    \u003cMibDataSync\u003e0\u003c/MibDataSync\u003e\n  \u003c/OntData\u003e\n\u003c/DslCpeConfig\u003e\n\n\nOnce the first create or set happens the omci library upon notification of the successful create-or-set will increment the value from 0 to 1 as seen here.   Independently the onu will also increment its value.\n\nThrough the course of successive creates/sets/deletes both the onu and the library will increment one by one.  When both the onu and library (independantly) reach 255, per the spec they both then jump from 255 to 1.  0 is specifically skipped as its reserved for the initial onu state or the result of a reset.",
      "parentUuid": "414db08d_942e796c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 227,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 227,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "9c0e958d16e392701542cdc5e1ba023dbd9c6d8b",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22adf6a1_2c204342",
